Puts your art on the real cards and shows you a screenshot of each as a reader sees it on a phone: up to {{ batch }} cards in one call. Code checks each piece first: printable ASCII only, at most {{ columns }} columns, any height, and how much of it is text and boxes: {% for kind in limits %}{{ kind.name }} at most {{ kind.words }} words (of two letters or more), letters at most {{ kind.letters }}% of its characters and box lines at most {{ kind.boxes }}%{% if not loop.last %}; {% endif %}{% endfor %}. A box line is + | = - # [ ], or any character of an outline with a word inside it, whatever it is drawn with; rows of one repeated character after the first are left out of the count. No row of # may stand in for text. A piece that fails isn't rendered, and the others are. Every render is a record. You see each screenshot only in this call's result, so judge it here: whether the picture reads at a glance, its labels and any line of dialogue are legible, and it sits well under the card's title.